{"vid":"orQKfIXMiA8","source":"orQKfIXMiA8.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"ARTHUR BROOKS: You need to be bored."},{"t":1.5,"txt":"You will have less meaning and you"},{"t":3.6,"txt":"will be more depressed if you never are bored."},{"t":5.8,"txt":"I mean, it couldn't be clearer."},{"t":10.1,"txt":"Let me give you the good side of boredom in general."},{"t":14.7,"txt":"Boredom is a tendency for us to not be occupied"},{"t":18.6,"txt":"otherwise cognitively, which switches over our thinking"},{"t":22.7,"txt":"system to use a part of our brain"},{"t":25,"txt":"that's called the default mode network."},{"t":27.1,"txt":"That sounds fancy."},{"t":28,"txt":"It's really not."},{"t":28.7,"txt":"The default mode network is a bunch"},{"t":30.2,"txt":"of structures in your brain that switch"},{"t":32.4,"txt":"on when you don't have anything else to think about."},{"t":35.6,"txt":"So you forgot your phone and you're sitting"},{"t":37.5,"txt":"at a light, for example."},{"t":39.6,"txt":"That's when your default mode network goes on."},{"t":42.5,"txt":"We don't like it."},{"t":43.7,"txt":"My colleague in the psychology department"},{"t":45.7,"txt":"here at Harvard, Dan Gilbert, he did experiments"},{"t":48.4,"txt":"where people had to sit in a room for 15"},{"t":50.8,"txt":"minutes with instructions to do absolutely nothing,"},{"t":53.1,"txt":"and there was nothing in the room to do,"},{"t":55.1,"txt":"except there was a button in front of them"},{"t":57.6,"txt":"that they could push."},{"t":58.5,"txt":"And if they did, they gave themselves"},{"t":60,"txt":"a painful electric shock."},{"t":62,"txt":"Sit there bored, or get a shock."},{"t":64.3,"txt":"A big majority of the participants"},{"t":65.8,"txt":"gave themselves shocks instead of thinking about nothing."},{"t":68.5,"txt":"We don't like boredom."},{"t":69.9,"txt":"Boredom is boredom is terrible."},{"t":71.3,"txt":"Why is boredom so bad?"},{"t":72.7,"txt":"Well, because the default mode network makes"},{"t":75.4,"txt":"us think about things that might be kind of uncomfortable."},{"t":78.3,"txt":"When you think about nothing while your mind wanders"},{"t":80.8,"txt":"and thinks about, for example, big questions of meaning"},{"t":83.6,"txt":"in your life."},{"t":84.2,"txt":"What does my life mean?"},{"t":85.3,"txt":"You go to uncomfortable existential questions"},{"t":88.4,"txt":"when you're bored."},{"t":89.7,"txt":"That turns out to be incredibly important, incredibly good."},{"t":92.6,"txt":"One of the reasons we have such an explosion of depression"},{"t":95,"txt":"and anxiety in our society today is because people actually"},{"t":98.9,"txt":"don't know the meaning of their lives,"},{"t":100.5,"txt":"much less so in previous generations."},{"t":102.4,"txt":"Tons of data show this, and furthermore, we're"},{"t":105.8,"txt":"not even looking."},{"t":106.8,"txt":"Why not?"},{"t":108.1,"txt":"I'll tell you why not."},{"t":109.3,"txt":"We figured out a way to eliminate boredom."},{"t":112.9,"txt":"We've been able, almost completely,"},{"t":116,"txt":"to shut off the default mode network in our brains."},{"t":119.2,"txt":"How?"},{"t":120.5,"txt":"The answer is that thing in your pocket with the screen,"},{"t":123.5,"txt":"which you take out even when you're standing on the street"},{"t":126.3,"txt":"corner waiting for the light to change,"},{"t":127.9,"txt":"is like, I might have to wait here for 15 seconds."},{"t":132.1,"txt":"What are you doing?"},{"t":132.9,"txt":"You're actually trying to not be bored because the default mode"},{"t":135.5,"txt":"network is mildly uncomfortable, because it sends you"},{"t":138.1,"txt":"to the types of questions that you can't get your mind around."},{"t":140.7,"txt":"You can't get your arms around."},{"t":142.1,"txt":"Well, that's a big problem."},{"t":143.7,"txt":"That's a doom loop of meaning."},{"t":146.3,"txt":"If every time you're slightly bored pull out your phone,"},{"t":149.6,"txt":"it's going to get harder and harder for you to find meaning,"},{"t":152.1,"txt":"and that's the recipe for depression and anxiety"},{"t":156.4,"txt":"and a sense of hollowness, which, by the way,"},{"t":159.5,"txt":"are all through the roof."},{"t":162.8,"txt":"I get it."},{"t":163.5,"txt":"You don't want to be bored."},{"t":164.8,"txt":"You need to be bored."},{"t":166.3,"txt":"Be bored more."},{"t":167.7,"txt":"Tomorrow, when you go to the gym in the morning"},{"t":169.7,"txt":"after you wake up, don't take your phone."},{"t":172.1,"txt":"Can you handle it?"},{"t":173.4,"txt":"Not listening to a podcast while you're working out."},{"t":176.4,"txt":"Just being in your head."},{"t":177.6,"txt":"I promise you, you'll have your most interesting ideas"},{"t":180.3,"txt":"while you're working out without devices."},{"t":182.1,"txt":"It's probably been a long time since you've done that."},{"t":184.3,"txt":"Commute with nothing, not even the radio."},{"t":187.1,"txt":"Can you do that?"},{"t":188.5,"txt":"Start getting better at periods that"},{"t":190.9,"txt":"are 15 minutes and longer of boredom,"},{"t":194,"txt":"and watch your life change."},{"t":196,"txt":"Number one, you'll be less bored with ordinary things"},{"t":198.6,"txt":"in your life."},{"t":199.2,"txt":"If you get better at the skill of boredom,"},{"t":201.2,"txt":"you'll be less bored with your job."},{"t":202.4,"txt":"You'll be less bored with your relationships."},{"t":204,"txt":"You'll be less bored with the things that"},{"t":205.7,"txt":"are going on around you."},{"t":207,"txt":"But more importantly, you'll start digging"},{"t":209.4,"txt":"into the biggest questions in your life, purpose, meaning,"},{"t":213.5,"txt":"coherence, significance."},{"t":217,"txt":"And who knows?"},{"t":218.1,"txt":"You might just get happier."},{"t":220.9,"txt":"People ask me all the time, is the doctor"},{"t":222.6,"txt":"taking his own prescriptions?"},{"t":224.6,"txt":"And the answer is, yes."},{"t":225.6,"txt":"Yes, I am."},{"t":226.7,"txt":"I'm prone to the same pathologies as anybody else"},{"t":229.2,"txt":"because I have the same brain chemistry as everybody else."},{"t":231.6,"txt":"So what do I do to fight that?"},{"t":232.8,"txt":"And the answer is, well, I do a number of things."},{"t":234.8,"txt":"I have a no device policy after 7:00 in the afternoon."},{"t":239.9,"txt":"I don't sleep with my phone."},{"t":241.5,"txt":"We don't have devices when we have meals in my family."},{"t":246.1,"txt":"Because we're there for each other."},{"t":247.8,"txt":"We're not there for people who aren't there."},{"t":250.6,"txt":"Three, I have regular social media"},{"t":252.8,"txt":"and screen cleanses where I don't use my device"},{"t":256.4,"txt":"for longer periods of time."},{"t":258.8,"txt":"First, it's like children screaming in my head"},{"t":262,"txt":"because that's how dopamine is saying, get the phone,"},{"t":265.6,"txt":"get the phone."},{"t":266.5,"txt":"That's addiction."},{"t":267.9,"txt":"But it calms down and I feel better."},{"t":270.4,"txt":"And I feel sort of blessed by the end."},{"t":273.3,"txt":"And I pick the phone up by the end"},{"t":275.1,"txt":"because I have to check my emails."},{"t":276.5,"txt":"And I have to be a normal, functioning, connected person"},{"t":279.4,"txt":"in the world."},{"t":280.3,"txt":"But it does remind me that my life doesn't have to revolve"},{"t":283.3,"txt":"around these devices."},{"t":284.3,"txt":"These protocols are really, really helpful"},{"t":286.7,"txt":"and I recommend them to anybody and everybody."},{"t":289.5,"txt":"Don't sleep with your phone."},{"t":290.8,"txt":"No phones during meals."},{"t":292.3,"txt":"Regular social media fasts."},{"t":294.6,"txt":"You'll get better."},{"t":296.8,"txt":"People worry that if they do these things,"},{"t":298.6,"txt":"they're going to miss something."},{"t":299.7,"txt":"There are ways that you can remedy that."},{"t":301.1,"txt":"One of the things that you can do"},{"t":302.4,"txt":"is you can have your phone on."},{"t":303.8,"txt":"You're just not looking at it, and there's"},{"t":305.6,"txt":"only one or two numbers that can reach you"},{"t":307.8,"txt":"in case of emergencies."},{"t":309.3,"txt":"Phones can do that by the way."},{"t":310.9,"txt":"If you don't have to do that, ask your kid."},{"t":313,"txt":"But don't use emergencies in as an excuse."},{"t":315.8,"txt":"Here's something that's not an emergency."},{"t":318.2,"txt":"What's going on Twitter."},{"t":319.9,"txt":"That's not an emergency answer nothing."},{"t":323,"txt":"It doesn't matter."},{"t":324.1,"txt":"The news can wait."},{"t":325.1,"txt":"Seriously your grandparents didn't"},{"t":327.2,"txt":"what was going on every single second in Washington, DC."},{"t":330.8,"txt":"You're killing yourself with this stuff."},{"t":333.4,"txt":"Are you kidding me?"},{"t":334.2,"txt":"It's bad for you."},{"t":335.8,"txt":"So let me say it straight to my kids."},{"t":338.7,"txt":"Put down your phones."},{"t":341.4,"txt":"You need more meaning in your life."},{"t":343.3,"txt":"And so do I."}],"words":[{"t":0,"w":"ARTHUR"},{"t":0,"w":"BROOKS:"},{"t":0,"w":"You"},{"t":0,"w":"need"},{"t":0,"w":"to"},{"t":0,"w":"be"},{"t":0,"w":"bored."},{"t":1.5,"w":"You"},{"t":1.5,"w":"will"},{"t":1.5,"w":"have"},{"t":1.5,"w":"less"},{"t":1.5,"w":"meaning"},{"t":1.5,"w":"and"},{"t":1.5,"w":"you"},{"t":3.56,"w":"will"},{"t":3.56,"w":"be"},{"t":3.56,"w":"more"},{"t":3.56,"w":"depressed"},{"t":3.56,"w":"if"},{"t":3.56,"w":"you"},{"t":3.56,"w":"never"},{"t":3.56,"w":"are"},{"t":3.56,"w":"bored."},{"t":5.778,"w":"I"},{"t":5.778,"w":"mean,"},{"t":5.778,"w":"it"},{"t":5.778,"w":"couldn't"},{"t":5.778,"w":"be"},{"t":5.778,"w":"clearer."},{"t":10.12,"w":"Let"},{"t":10.12,"w":"me"},{"t":10.12,"w":"give"},{"t":10.12,"w":"you"},{"t":10.12,"w":"the"},{"t":10.12,"w":"good"},{"t":10.12,"w":"side"},{"t":10.12,"w":"of"},{"t":10.12,"w":"boredom"},{"t":10.12,"w":"in"},{"t":10.12,"w":"general."},{"t":14.68,"w":"Boredom"},{"t":14.68,"w":"is"},{"t":14.68,"w":"a"},{"t":14.68,"w":"tendenc